A copy of lib/rbcodec/codecs/libtremor (Xiph's Tremor, BSD-style licence,
see COPYING) and the headers of the MDCT it uses from lib/rbcodec/codecs/lib
(mdct.h, fft.h, mdct_lookup.h, codeclib_misc.h; the code itself is the copy
in faad/lib, which the AAC decoder already builds), built into the GabagoolOS interface to decode Ogg Vorbis internet
radio. vorbisfile.c and ctype.c are left out (the radio reads Ogg pages
itself). Changes from the Rockbox copy: codeclib.h here is a shim for the
codec interface (plain malloc, no IRAM, the transforms' prototypes, the byte
order from the compiler), oggmalloc.c allocates from the C library, the ARM
and ColdFire assembly headers are not included, and mdct_lookup.c includes
the shim outside Rockbox builds too.
